# MediaPipe source we build from. The Apache-2.0 source is telemetry-free;
# Google injects the clearcut phone-home only into their own pip wheels
# (see google-ai-edge/mediapipe#6291). Building from this commit gives us the
# latest functionality without the tracking.
#
# v1.0.0, not 1.0.1: PyPI serves a 1.0.1 wheel (2026-08-14) but upstream has
# never tagged that source — the newest tag is v1.0.0 (2026-07-28), and a wheel
# can only be built from a source release we can name. The version we publish is
# therefore v1.0.0 until Google tags again.
#
# v1.0.0 is bzlmod-first: its own .bazelrc sets `common --enable_bzlmod` and it
# ships MODULE.bazel *and* WORKSPACE. That is why the 0.10.35 recipe's
# `--noenable_bzlmod` workaround is gone — the flag was the class of failure
# behind all five dead runs of September 2026 (`No repository visible as
# '@flatbuffers'`).
source  = https://github.com/google-ai-edge/mediapipe
tag     = v1.0.0
commit  = 6d31f1ebc3284db74d211d62bdc4f0a0c29ea120
version = 1.0.0
